# .gitleaksignore — synthetic test fixtures, not real secrets.
#
# The paths below contain INTENTIONALLY-FAKE credentials used as positive
# test fixtures for NEKOWORK's secret-detection rules (hardcoded-credential,
# secret-fallback). They are crafted to look like real AWS keys, GitHub PATs,
# private keys, JWT-secret fallbacks, etc. so the rules can be exercised against
# realistic input. None of them are live or grant access to anything. Listing
# them here prevents gitleaks from flagging the deliberately-fake fixtures.
#
# Path globs (gitleaks honours glob patterns in .gitleaksignore in addition to
# commit:file:rule:line fingerprints). If your gitleaks version requires
# fingerprints, mirror these directories under [allowlist] paths in your
# gitleaks config.

# Hardcoded-credential positives (fake AWS/GitHub/Google/SendGrid/Twilio/etc.)
packages/nekowork/tests/fixtures/hardcoded-credential/positive/**

# Secret-fallback positives (env-var || "literal-default" patterns)
packages/nekowork/tests/fixtures/secret-fallback/positive/**

# Scraped OSS candidate fixtures + captured live-AI diffs for the above rules
packages/nekowork/tests/fixtures/secret-fallback/positive/candidates/**
packages/nekowork/tests/fixtures/secret-fallback/positive/live-ai/**
